interfaces:
**Wire (SPA to BFF to model-gateway `POST /v1/invoke/stream` body), added key:** `execute_granted: true` (the alias `executeGranted` is accepted by the gateway). It is present only on an execute turn, together with `features` containing `agentic`, `plan_mode:false`, and a non-empty `thread_id` of an existing thread. No rung, plan id or grant data is on the wire.

**Typed refusal (SSE `error` event):** `{code:"plan_grant_unavailable", retryable:false}`. It is emitted when no live grant exists for (verified org, `run.thread_id`). The run is terminalized with failure code `dispatch_rejected` (already allowlisted) and execution-core is never called. A malformed combination returns `{code:"invalid_request"}` before any run exists. A ZDR token returns the existing `zdr_feature_not_supported` with feature `agentic`.

**Plan-approval response (additive):** `"grant_expires_at_unix": <i64>|null`, proxied by the BFF unchanged.

